			<div class="content" id="post-content-3875781">
									

<p>I have a few reservations.</p>
<p>I was never too familiar with the canons involving <em>Solidarity</em>, but you should probably at least link the <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/stealingsolidarityhub">Stealing Solidarity Hub</a> somewhere in this article.</p>
<p>I was left uncertain as to what caused the ship to go into disarray with the BRC still alive and no threat left to fight. I assume this was explained in the aforementioned hub, but I don't know. I was expecting an <em>Aliens</em> situation.</p>
<p>This new article feels like a prologue. I was hoping that the BRC and The Foundation would team up against some big bad in this. Maybe in the future, or is there a hub for this already (and if so can we have a link to it in this article)?</p>
<p>Finally&#8230; is this article&#8230; allowed? A loophole is being exploited here. On one hand I'm happy that the <em>Solidarity</em> is back, and on the other hand it feels disrespectful. Did Von Pincier allow this, or does his opinion not matter in this regard? Trudging into new territory I suppose&#8230;</p>

